 ## Overview
-A ray-marching technique for volume rendering that combines a Discrete Differential Analyzer (DDA) for traversing a coarse spatial partition (macrocells) with Delta Tracking (Russian Roulette) for sampling absorption and scattering events within those cells [S1, unofficial]. It handles sparse or heterogeneous media by skipping empty macrocells and using a majorant density [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard DDA by replacing uniform step sizes with probabilistic free-flight distances derived from the majorant, allowing it to skip non-interacting regions within a macrocell more efficiently than fixed-step marching, while avoiding the overhead of full per-voxel traversal [G]. It builds on [Macrocell Grid Traversal with Majorant Densities](1528-macrocell-grid-traversal-with-majorant-densities.md).
+A ray-marching technique for volume rendering that combines a Discrete Differential Analyzer (DDA) for traversing a coarse spatial partition (macrocells) with Delta Tracking (Russian Roulette) for sampling absorption and scattering events within those cells [S1, unofficial]. It handles sparse or heterogeneous media by skipping empty macrocells and using a majorant density [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard DDA by replacing uniform step sizes with probabilistic free-flight distances derived from the majorant, allowing it to skip non-interacting regions within a macrocell more efficiently than fixed-step marching, while avoiding the overhead of full per-voxel traversal [G]. It builds on [Macrocell Grid Traversal with Majorant Densities](1528-macrocell-grid-traversal-with-majorant-densities.md) [G].
 
